cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "attribution-calibration: error rates for directed attribution claims about multi-agent logs"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jacob
    given-names: Manu Nicholas
    email: manunicholasjacob@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
abstract: >-
  A detector-agnostic harness that attaches an error rate to a directed attribution or influence
  claim about a multi-agent log. The user supplies their own detector and their own event log and
  gets back a family-wise error rate measured on surrogates built from that same log, a power curve
  from a spike-in positive control, and a detection floor reported with an explicit status. Every
  rate carries a Wilson interval. Four surrogates are provided, including the conventional
  circular-shift recipe, which is implemented faithfully in order to be measured against: it does
  not hold the actor sequence fixed, and on turn-ordered agent chat it was found to certify at least
  one influence edge on 90 per cent of structure-free replicates against a nominal 5 per cent.
keywords:
  - attribution
  - influence detection
  - multi-agent systems
  - surrogate data
  - family-wise error
  - statistical power
  - AI safety
  - calibration
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/attribution-calibration"
url: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/attribution-calibration"
